Example 1: With number 528,103

10
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:40,620
Observe table beside together

11
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:59,930
Whole part has ones, tens, hundreds

12
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:12,130
Decimal part has tenths, hundredths, thousandths

13
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:17,620
Relationship

14
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:29,280
Whole part: Each unit of a place equals 10 units of immediately lower place..

15
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:42,040
Decimal part: Each unit of a place equals 1/10 (or 0.1) unit of immediately higher place.

16
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:52,460
